# The build context is the repository root, and `make build` on a host sends
# all of it to the daemon. Without this, that includes .env — every secret the
# stack has — and however many gigabytes of Airflow task logs have accumulated.
#
# A deploy's build does not have this problem, because it builds from a fresh
# git worktree where none of these exist. That difference is precisely why the
# gap is easy to miss.

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.git/
.github/
terraform/
docs/

# Runtime state, rebuildable
airflow/logs/
quality/gx_output/
metabase/.state/
.scratch/

# Local development
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
node_modules/
*.duckdb
*.duckdb.wal

.DS_Store
